# Prefer Cursor native modes (P1 — orchestrate, don't replace)

cstl **prefers** Cursor's built-in modes and maps them to Trellis Triage/phases. **Do not replace** Cursor UI. Full table + citations: `.cstl/spec/guides/cursor-native-modes-guide.md` · evidence: `{TASK}/research/cursor-modes-external.md`.

## Quick routing

| Situation | Prefer | Trellis anchor |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Read-only explain / lookup | **Ask** (`Shift+Tab`) | `[Triage: No Task]` — no edits; side chat OK for tangents during Agent |
| Scope / design before code | **Plan** | Phase 1; **Save to workspace** → `prd.md` / `design.md` / `implement.md`; then `--check` |
| Approved build / verify | **Agent** | Phase 2–3; `execution_mode`; `SwitchMode` → agent after Plan |
| Runtime / repeat failure | **Debug** (`Shift+Tab`) | Evidence → `verify.md`; `cstl-break-loop` if looped |
| Independent Parent children (post-approval) | **Multitask** / Build in Parallel | Explicit `.cstl/tasks/<dir>` per worker; Parent integrates |

## Hard boundaries

- Plan default save = **home dir** — not Trellis task paths until user saves/maps.
- Multitask/subagents: **never** rely on `selected_task`; no collision guarantee — worktrees + Parent review.
- Agent `SwitchMode`: **plan/agent only**; Ask/Debug = user `Shift+Tab` / picker.

